      "id": "wqwow9o",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Background of Panchayati Raj"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Panchayati Raj System was granted constitutional status under Part IX through the 73rd Constitutional Amendment Act.",
        "The structure consists of a three-tier setup: Gram Panchayat at the village level, Panchayat Samiti at the block level, and Zila Parishad at the district level.",
        "Gram Sabha serves as the primary body composed of all registered voters in the village.",
        "The 11th Schedule enumerates 29 functional matters entrusted to the Panchayats."
      ],
      "id": "z5u82uv"
    },
